{"uid":"61e45cb714196e29","name":"test_pytest_collection_with_decoy_ahead_of_repo_on_pythonpath_still_resolves_here","fullName":"tests.test_tests_conftest_resolution#test_pytest_collection_with_decoy_ahead_of_repo_on_pythonpath_still_resolves_here","historyId":"66a1bcf170aa0127db3bc9c4ef2585b6","time":{"start":1791938088926,"stop":1791938090130,"duration":1204},"description":"A decoy `tests` *namespace portion* reachable via `PYTHONPATH` (the\n    scenario a stray dev-tooling entry, or another checked-out project,\n    could produce) must not shadow this repo's `tests.conftest` when pytest\n    collects a real test module. With `python -m pytest`, the working\n    directory ('') already sits ahead of `PYTHONPATH` entries on\n    `sys.path`, so *resolution* in this scenario survives even with\n    `/conftest.py` deleted -- what does not survive is the exact-`__path__`\n    invariant asserted in `test_fixture_uses_this_repos_conftest` (without\n    the pre-bind, the decoy's directory joins the merged namespace\n    `__path__` as a second portion, so a `tests.*` submodule this repo does\n    *not* ship could still be served from the decoy). The harder orderings\n    and the harder decoy shape are the tests below.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>A decoy <code>tests</code> <em>namespace portion</em> reachable via <code>PYTHONPATH</code> (the<br />\nscenario a stray dev-tooling entry, or another checked-out project,<br />\ncould produce) must not shadow this repo's <code>tests.conftest</code> when pytest<br />\ncollects a real test module. With <code>python -m pytest</code>, the working<br />\ndirectory ('') already sits ahead of <code>PYTHONPATH</code> entries on<br />\n<code>sys.path</code>, so <em>resolution</em> in this scenario survives even with<br />\n<code>/conftest.py</code> deleted -- what does not survive is the exact-<code>__path__</code><br />\ninvariant asserted in <code>test_fixture_uses_this_repos_conftest</code> (without<br />\nthe pre-bind, the decoy's dire